      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ إِنَّ رَجُلاً اِسْتَشَارَنِي فِي اَلْحَجِّ وَ كَانَ ضَعِيفَ اَلْحَالِ فَأَشَرْتُ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ لاَ يَحُجَّ فَقَالَ «مَا أَخْلَقَكَ أَنْ تَمْرَضَ سَنَةً» فَقَالَ فَمَرِضْتُ سَنَةً."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2234 - It is narrated from Ishaq ibn Ammar, who said: \"I said to Abu Abdullah (Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq), peace be upon him: 'A man consulted me about performing Hajj, and he was in a weak financial state, so I advised him not to perform Hajj.'\nThe Imam (as) replied: 'How fitting it would be for you to fall ill for a year.'\nIshaq said: 'And so I did fall ill for a year.'\""
        ]
      }
